  "tutorialTempoTitle": "Tempo, beats, and the pendulum",
  "tutorialTempoBody": "The pendulum swings once per beat. The big number is the tempo in BPM, or beats per minute. The row of dots shows where you are in the bar, and the brightest dot is the accented downbeat.",
  "tutorialTempoExample": "60 BPM = 1 beat per second\n120 BPM = 2 beats per second (twice as fast)",
  "tutorialBpmDragTitle": "Set the tempo",
  "tutorialBpmDragBody": "Pick a tempo where you can play every note correctly, then raise it once that feels easy. The slider runs from 30 to 240.",
  "tutorialBpmDragAction": "drag the tempo slider to any value.",
  "tutorialSequenceTitle": "Your note pattern",
  "tutorialSequenceBody": "This metronome does more than click. It plays your note pattern as a melody, one note per beat, looping while you play along. This panel shows the pattern loaded right now. Tap it to edit the notes.",
  "tutorialToggleTitle": "Click and Sound",
  "tutorialToggleBody": "\"Click\" is the classic tick that keeps time. \"Sound\" plays your note pattern on the selected instrument. Keep both on to hear the melody over the beat, or turn one off to focus on the other.",
  "tutorialToggleAction": "turn one switch off, then on again.",
  "tutorialMeterTitle": "Meter and subdivision",
  "tutorialMeterBody": "The time signature groups beats into bars. In 4/4 you count 1-2-3-4 and start over, and beat 1 gets the accent. Subdivision splits each beat into smaller clicks, which helps when your notes move faster than the beat.",
  "tutorialMeterExample": "4/4 = 4 beats per bar, the most common\n3/4 = counts in 3, like a waltz\nEighth subdivision = 2 clicks per beat",
  "tutorialTransportTitle": "Hear it",
  "tutorialTransportBody": "Everything is set. Press Start and listen: the accented first beat, then your notes landing on each beat. Stop pauses the session, and Reset returns to the beginning of your pattern.",
  "tutorialTransportAction": "press Start and listen for a bar or two.",
  "tutorialAdvancedTitle": "Advanced settings",
  "tutorialAdvancedBody": "When the defaults feel limiting, open this panel to change the click sound, choose the instrument that plays your notes, adjust accents, or shift the base octave.",
  "tutorialHomePracticeTitle": "Welcome. Practice starts here",
  "tutorialHomePracticeBody": "Metrinote is a metronome that also plays the notes you want to practice, so you hear the beat and the melody together. This button opens the practice page with your current note pattern loaded.",
  "tutorialHomeHistoryTitle": "Practice history",
  "tutorialHomeHistoryBody": "Every session is recorded here: minutes practiced over the last 7 days, your most used tempo, and your most used instrument. Set a daily goal and the progress ring shows how far along you are.",
  "tutorialHomeTabsTitle": "Four tabs",
  "tutorialHomeTabsBody": "Practice is the main page. Sequences is where you create and save note patterns. Tools generates patterns for you. Basics explains the music terms this app uses. Let's go through them in order.",
  "tutorialHomeExamplesTitle": "Start from an example",
  "tutorialHomeExamplesBody": "Not sure what to practice? These ready-made patterns load with one tap, including a Western major scale and an Eastern raga cycle. Load one, then change it into your own.",
  "tutorialHomeSequencesTitle": "Write your own pattern",
  "tutorialHomeSequencesBody": "Type note names separated by spaces, or tap the note buttons below the field. Western letters (A B C…) and Eastern sargam (S R G M…) both work. Give the pattern a name and save it to load again later.",
  "tutorialHomeSequencesExample": "C D E F → four notes, one per beat\nG - → '-' holds G for an extra beat\nE/F → '/' fits two notes into one beat\nC' high octave · C, low octave",
  "tutorialHomeToolsTitle": "Let Tools generate patterns",
  "tutorialHomeToolsBody": "The Tools tab has two generators: a scale builder and a jianpu converter. Both write patterns for you. Let's look at each.",
  "tutorialHomeScaleGenTitle": "Scale pattern generator",
  "tutorialHomeScaleGenBody": "Pick a root key, scale type, octave range, and direction, and it writes the full pattern. \"Use as Sequence\" drops the result into your sequence editor.",
  "tutorialHomeJianpuTitle": "Jianpu converter",
  "tutorialHomeJianpuBody": "If you read numbered notation (1 2 3 = do re mi), paste it here and it becomes a playable pattern. Octave dots and dashes for held notes are recognized too.",
  "tutorialHomeBasicsTitle": "Learn the terms",
  "tutorialHomeBasicsBody": "One more stop. Basics is a plain-language glossary of every music term this app uses. Let's read the four most important ones.",
  "tutorialBasicsBpmBody": "BPM means beats per minute, so 60 BPM is exactly one beat every second. This is the number you set with the tempo slider on the practice page. The rule of thumb is to start slower than feels comfortable.",
  "tutorialBasicsMeterBody": "The top number says how many beats each bar contains, and beat 1 always gets the accent. You choose it with the meter button on the practice page. For most music 4/4 is a safe default.",
  "tutorialBasicsSubdivisionBody": "Subdivision splits each beat into smaller equal clicks: eighths give 2 clicks per beat, sixteenths give 4. Turn it on when your notes move faster than the main beat.",
  "tutorialBasicsNotationBody": "The same notes have two naming systems, and this app accepts both: Western letters (C D E F G A B) and Eastern sargam (S R G M P D N). The nearby cards also cover octave marks, held notes, and grouping.",
  "tutorialHomeReturnTitle": "Back to the main page",
  "tutorialHomeReturnBody": "That's all four tabs. Tap Practice yourself to return to the main page, so you always know how to get back.",
  "tutorialStartSessionTitle": "Start when you're ready",
  "tutorialStartSessionBody": "Now press Start Metronome. That opens the practice page, where the hands-on metronome tutorial continues.",
  "tutorialHomeSettingsTitle": "Settings and replay",
  "tutorialHomeSettingsBody": "Theme, colors, and language live behind this gear. If you ever forget how something works, open Settings and tap \"Replay tutorial\". Press Done and we'll return to Practice.",
  "tutorialScoreTitle": "Sheet music in landscape",
  "tutorialScoreBody": "On larger screens in landscape, load a sheet-music image or PDF here and practice with the metronome beside it. You can zoom, flip pages, and go fullscreen.",
